---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import IconBadge from '../components/IconBadge.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About SM Global Accounting Services"
  description="Meet the outsourced accounting team supporting UK accountancy practices with statutory accounts, personal tax and bookkeeping — GDPR-compliant, UK GAAP-trained, and built to work as an extension of your firm."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">About Us</p>
      <h1>An Extension of Your Practice, Not a Replacement for It</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        SM Global Accounting Services is an outsourcing partnership built specifically around the needs
        of UK accountancy practices. We handle the statutory accounts, personal tax, bookkeeping and
        compliance workload that takes up your team's time — so your practice can focus on advisory
        work and client relationships, the parts of the job that actually need to happen in-house.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What We Believe</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="lock" />
          <h3>Your data is not ours to risk</h3>
          <p>Every process is built around keeping client data inside your own systems.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="shield" />
          <h3>Outsourcing should feel invisible to your clients</h3>
          <p>We work under your brand, your templates, and your quality standards.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="heart" />
          <h3>Good outsourcing is a relationship, not a transaction</h3>
          <p>Dedicated teams, regular check-ins, and a named point of contact — not a ticket queue.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="bolt" />
          <h3>We're never done learning</h3>
          <p>Compliance rules, software and best practice keep changing, so we treat staying current as part of the job, not an afterthought. We're not a rigid team — when there's a better way to do something, we adopt it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Trained on the Standards You Work To</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Our accountants and bookkeepers are trained on UK GAAP — including FRS 102 (Section 1A) and
        FRS 105 for small companies and micro-entities — alongside Making Tax Digital requirements,
        current HMRC filing deadlines, and Companies House statutory obligations. We're not adapting
        a generic process to UK rules; UK compliance is the process.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>From One Client's Trust to a Full-Service Firm</h2>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 720px;">
        It started with one freelancer, one client, and a blank page. A UK accountancy practice had
        just been incorporated — nothing was built yet — and needed someone who could turn that
        blank page into a working firm: company processes, internal workflow, company secretarial
        and administrative work, tax setup, and the year-end and bookkeeping software stack, all
        built from scratch.
      </p>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 720px;">
        The client noticed. Enough to hand over their entire processing workload to the person who'd
        built it. That trust is what turned freelance work into something bigger — a subcontractor
        came on board, then joined as a full employee, and one freelancer's workload grew into a
        firm's.
      </p>
      <p class="lead" style="max-width: 720px;">
        We formally became SM Global Accounting Services in 2025 to carry that work forward properly,
        and the team has grown from one person to a small team since — without losing the hands-on
        way of working that got us here. Today, we support that same practice's accounting workload —
        around 120–130 clients across the UK, US, UAE and beyond — handling everything from AML
        screening, client onboarding, company incorporation and company secretarial work through to
        bookkeeping, statutory accounts and filing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Meet the Team</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Real qualifications, not just job titles — this is the team actually preparing your files.
      </p>
      <div class="grid grid--2" style="margin-top: var(--space-3);">
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="badge-check" />
          <h3>Account Manager</h3>
          <p>ACCA-certified, with 7+ years' experience in the financial field — oversees the relationship and day-to-day priorities.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="heart" />
          <h3>Relationship Manager</h3>
          <p>A dedicated person who builds and maintains the relationship — with the client, and between our own team members.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="users" />
          <h3>Client Manager &amp; Senior Accountant</h3>
          <p>ACCA Affiliate — leads day-to-day client work alongside senior-level review of files.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="briefcase" />
          <h3>Senior Accountants</h3>
          <p>ACCA and CA Affiliate, with 10+ years' experience — handle the core preparation work: bookkeeping, VAT, year-end accounts and tax computations.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <IconBadge name="document" />
          <h3>Junior Accountants</h3>
          <p>3+ years' experience — support the preparation and processing work behind every file.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <CtaBand headline="Want to See How We'd Fit Into Your Practice?" />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
